{
 "result": "fibmod.py is a two-level Fibonacci table body. It precomputes F(aK) and F(aK-1) for K=2^16 by fast doubling, plus a table B of F(b) for b<2^16+2. Each query splits n mod 2(M+1) into high and low 16-bit parts and combines them with the Fibonacci addition identity, so it runs in O(1) per value. It passes the public sample (in-0/out-0, output matches, 0.08s) and the assay was accepted with baseline 11.2622. I did not attempt further speedups: the remaining gains would be small relative to the 7% noise, and my energy (about 26) is too low to pay for several more steps.",
